==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|physics}} Potential [[energy]] (not force) divided by [[electric]] [[charge]]; measured in [[volt]]s

====Usage notes====
Despite the name, ''electromotive force'' is related to potential energy rather than force. To avoid confusion, [[w:International Organization for Standardization|ISO]] and [[w:International Electrotechnical Commission|IEC]] standards recommend using the terms ''source voltage'' or ''source tension'' instead.<ref>{{cite-web|title=IEC 60050 - International Electrotechnical Vocabulary - Details for IEV number 131-12-22: "source voltage" |url=https://www.electropedia.org/iev/iev.nsf/display?openform&ievref=131-12-22 |access-date=2022-12-19 |website=www.electropedia.org}}</ref><ref name=80000-6:2022>{{cite-web|title=IEC 80000-6:2022|url=https://www.iso.org/standard/77846.html|publisher=[[w:International Organization for Standardization|International Organization for Standardization]]|access-date=2022-12-19}}</ref>

